  "conclusions": [
    "Each map iterator ultimately returns node+8 as pair payload; its map operator[] returns payload+4 at918B46/918C74/918DA4, so key=node+8/value=node+C.",
    "Each map clear resets sentinel.next/sentinel.prev to head, count map+4 to0 and walks node.next, corroborating circular element-list header layout.",
    "CString/int vector append methods read begin+0/end+4/capacity+8 and advance end by4. The outer map value atnode+C is a12-byte vector header; 4-byte CString storage or int32 elements are selected by the concrete map source."
